module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LimitApproxClose.Exists
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LimitApproxClose.StageDiagram

/-!
# The index of pairs still works for charted subalgebras

The index preorder of the one-affine-open step of Tag 07RN is the pairs `(k, A)` consisting of a
stage `k` and a *distinguished* subalgebra `A` of the ring at that stage, and
`Stacks.StageSubalgebra.isDirected` makes it a nonempty directed preorder as soon as the
distinguished subalgebras are finitely generated and cofinal among the finitely generated ones.
In the existing specialization the distinguished subalgebras are the finite-type open models of
Tag 01Z7, which is the predicate that does **not** determine the image of the factorization it
provides.

This file records that nothing is lost by strengthening the predicate to the *charted*
subalgebras of `AlgebraicGeometry.IsChartedSubalgebra`, which do determine that image: charted
subalgebras are finitely generated by definition and cofinal by
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isChartedSubalgebra_ge`, so the index built from them is still a
nonempty directed preorder with cofinal projection to the stages.

That is the one thing a reader should check before the strengthening is used: the image equality
is bought by asking more of `A`, and asking more of `A` could have cost the directedness of the
index, which is what makes the extended system a directed inverse system at all.

## What is proved, and the route

* `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.isDirected_isChartedSubalgebra` and
  `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.nonempty_isChartedSubalgebra` are
  `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.isDirected` and `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.nonempty` fed with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isChartedSubalgebra_ge`, whose conclusion is already in the shape
  the cofinality hypothesis asks for.  Nonemptiness is cofinality above the bottom subalgebra,
  which is finitely generated.

* `Stacks.StageSubalgebra.exists_le_proj_isChartedSubalgebra` is the cofinality of the
  projection to the stages, specialized; it is what
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.FiniteTypeApproximation.comp` asks of an index map.

## Universe situation

The stages, the rings and the schemes share the universe `u`, inherited from the general index.
The charting families are indexed by a fixed `Fin n`, which is where they come from in the
application: the finitely many standard opens of the affine open being added.

## Transparency gotchas

The hypothesis of the cofinality is a *stagewise* family of charting elements together with
finite type of each of their localizations; the latter is where the geometry enters, through
`AlgebraicGeometry.finiteType_localization_away_of_basicOpen_le`, and it is deliberately left as
a hypothesis here so that this file mentions no scheme.

## What is NOT done here

The charting families at the several stages are *not* required to be compatible with the
transition maps, and nothing here says they can be chosen so.  That compatibility is what the
gluing needs on top of the image equality, and it is not proved anywhere yet.  Nothing here
builds the second leg of the glueing, a cone, a limit, or an inhabitant of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.FiniteTypeApproximation`.  Tag 07RN is not proved and no tag attribute
is attached to anything in this file.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07RN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07RN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Z7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Z7)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.StageSubalgebra

variable {K : Type u} [Preorder K] (F : K ⥤ CommRingCat.{u}) {n : ℕ}
  (r : ∀ k : K, Fin n → F.obj k)
  (hft : ∀ (k : K) (l : Fin n), Algebra.FiniteType ℤ (Localization.Away (r k l)))

include hft

/-- Every stage has a charted subalgebra. -/
private lemma exists_isChartedSubalgebra (k : K) :
    ∃ A : Subalgebra ℤ (F.obj k), IsChartedSubalgebra A (r k) :=
  (exists_isChartedSubalgebra_ge (r k) (hft k) ⊥ Subalgebra.fg_bot).imp fun _ h ↦ h.1

/-- **The index of pairs is nonempty for charted subalgebras.** -/
lemma nonempty_isChartedSubalgebra [Nonempty K] :
    Nonempty (StageSubalgebra F fun k A ↦ IsChartedSubalgebra A (r k)) :=
  nonempty (exists_isChartedSubalgebra F r hft)

/-- **The projection to the stages is cofinal for charted subalgebras.** -/
lemma exists_le_proj_isChartedSubalgebra (k : K) :
    ∃ j : StageSubalgebra F fun k A ↦ IsChartedSubalgebra A (r k), k ≤ proj j :=
  exists_le_proj (exists_isChartedSubalgebra F r hft) k

/-- **The index of pairs is directed for charted subalgebras.**  Charted subalgebras are
finitely generated by definition and cofinal among the finitely generated ones, which is exactly
what the directedness of the index asks of a predicate. -/
lemma isDirected_isChartedSubalgebra [IsDirected K (· ≤ ·)] :
    IsDirected (StageSubalgebra F fun k A ↦ IsChartedSubalgebra A (r k)) (· ≤ ·) :=
  isDirected (fun _ _ h ↦ h.fg) fun k C hC ↦ exists_isChartedSubalgebra_ge (r k) (hft k) C hC

end Stacks.StageSubalgebra
